+For a judge or an engineer who has cloned the repository. After the one-time install, the walk-through below takes about two minutes by hand. It needs no key and no `.env`: with the helper off, which is the default, no model is called anywhere.
+
+1. **Install and start it.** Follow "Getting it running" in the README: the virtual environment, `pip install -r backend/requirements-dev.txt`, `npm install` in `frontend`, then the backend and `npm run dev` in two terminals. Open `http://localhost:5173`. On macOS or Linux, read `.venv/bin/python` where the README says `.venv/Scripts/python.exe`.
+2. **Choose English.** A clean browser opens in Hindi; use the language menu in the bar at the top.
+3. **Enter the example of section 10.2.** Press "Start my journey", then answer:
+   - "Tell us about yourself": any name, then "Continue to my business".
+   - "Tell us what you do": "What is your business called?" any name, which stays in the browser; "What kind of work is it?" "Tailoring / Garments"; "How much money do you require?" 200000; "How much money do you expect to earn each month?" 30000; "How much will the business itself cost each month?" 15000; then "Continue to my area".
+   - "Where does your business operate?": Uttar Pradesh, Lucknow, "Village / Rural"; then "Continue to finance".
+   - "Let us understand your finances": "How much money do you already have?" 150000; "How much do you spend each month?" 18000; leave "Do you or your family repay any loan or EMI?" closed, because the example repays none; "How much does your household earn in a month?" 25000; tick the consent box; then "Check my business".
+4. **Read the result.** The page opens on "Simple": the light is yellow ("Yellow: something to check before you go ahead"), because the figures work but ₹50,000 of the money to start is missing, and the page keeps the main figures and what to do next. Press "Detailed" at the top (the choice stays for the next page) to see "Loan pressure 9.27%", 14 matched schemes and the number of tailoring businesses registered in Lucknow, from data.gov.in. Press "See advice" for the loans of 12, 24, 36 and 60 months (24 months: ₹50,000 at ₹2,354 a month), what PMEGP and Mudra would put in and add, and the four registrations to ask about. "Make my report" adds the month-by-month schedule. Section 10.4 lists every figure. The switch "How much to show" hides the working; a clean browser opens on "Simple".
+5. **Check that no model computes anything.** `cd backend && ../.venv/Scripts/python.exe -m pytest tests/test_model_boundary.py -q` runs 25 tests that fail if a rule module under `backend/app/services/` imports the Meta client or anything that opens a connection. `pytest tests -q` in the same folder runs all 2,245.
+6. **What needs a key.** Only `/talk` (spoken or typed intake) and the written-plan card. Both stay hidden unless the server has `ARTHNITI_AI_ENABLED=true` and `MODEL_API_KEY` and the frontend build has `VITE_AI_HELPER=true`. The README's "The voice and text helper (optional)" has the steps and a capped smoke test, and the video shows both.
+7. **What is new, and what is not claimed.** Section 2.3 shows how to diff against the start of the event. The pages say the rest themselves: no scheme's eligibility is checked, every loan and scheme figure is an estimate and not an offer, the light reads only the figures typed in, and the wording in the seven languages other than English is machine-written and has not been reviewed by native speakers.
